A||||3||RiceBurner515||engine light, where?||||8||
Z||000000||RiceBurner515||11-10-2000||03:56 PM||||where exactly is the engine light supposed to be on the instrument panel? i think i have a light out or someone did something to make it not go on...where should it be, its not lighting up when i start the engine nor when i do an ECM test?||||reg||8
Z||000001||Old Lar||11-10-2000||04:12 PM||||There are 6 squares in the center of the dash.  The lower right one is the Service Engine one.  It should go on when you start the car.  Some people who sell their Fieros with engine light problems remove the bulb, clip a wire or if they are really lazy, cover it with black tape.  All the idiot lights should go on when you turn the key on, prior to starting the car to insre the lights are working.||||reg||4
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||11-10-2000||04:13 PM||||Its the bottom dummy light on the right side.<P>Your light bulb may be burnt out. The easy way to change it is to take the panel off behind you speedo cluster. 3 torx screws on top, 2 behind & 2 under the dash/cluster. When you have the panel off wiggle the socket. It may just be loose.<BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlogo1_1.gif">   <BR><B>"AHHHHH!!! All Fiero's don't start on fire you BONEHEAD!!"</B>||||reg||10
Z||000003||theogre||11-10-2000||06:10 PM||||The ECM light should be on durring lamp test. If it's not then it's a lamp issue.<P>Actually, unless the wiring has been corrected the Temp light does not light durring lamp test. <P>There is no lamp test for Seatbelt.The Seatbelt light won't light at all if the chime unit is out or dead. It lights for 10 seconds when the key goes from off to run.<P>||||reg||4
